    ],
    "structure_function_summary": "Driven heavily by β-caryophyllene and limonene, this profile is primarily being studied for its potential to support healthy inflammatory responses and robust cellular antioxidant defenses. Researchers are exploring whether this specific combination of terpenes might work together to support physical comfort, balanced mood, and neurological health. The strongest foundational research for these combined effects comes from human clinical trials (Oxford level 1b), offering an exciting glimpse into how these botanical compounds interact with human biology.",
    "evidence_at_a_glance": "The strongest evidence behind these dominant compounds includes human clinical trials (Oxford level 1b) for β-caryophyllene's neuroprotective and comfort-supporting properties, though it is important to note that clinical study doses differ significantly from the milligrams found in a standard serving.",
    "minor_notes": "The long tail of this profile is remarkably diverse, featuring 120 identified compounds including a notable 4.97 percent share of linalool, a floral molecule backed by human trials for its calming and antimicrobial potential, as well as the fascinating insect-signaling pheromone (E)-β-farnesene."
  }
